  "number": 811,
  "state": "closed",
  "locked": false,
  "title": "Skip the free-slot suspension while a Session waits for its sandbox",
  "user": {
    "login": "SaladDay",
    "id": 92240037,
    "node_id": "U_kgDOBX94pQ",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92240037?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/SaladDay",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "## What users see\n\nA new hosted Session placed on a full node no longer waits behind a free-slot suspension. On the test cluster one Session waited 6.6 s for it.\n\n## Cause\n\nA placement counts as active before its sandbox exists. Right after a Session was placed on a node, the node looked full again, and the node lane, still in the same scan, found an allocation idle for over 2 minutes and suspended it under the free-slot rule. The lane creates sandboxes only between scans, so the placed Session's sandbox came after that suspension.\n\nmx test, Core log (UTC): S1's allocation suspended at 15:17:52.450, S3 was placed on the freed slot, then `fc970892` (idle since a regression case) started quiescing at 15:17:52.558 and was suspended at 15:17:59.152; S3's create started at 15:17:59.19.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `placement.Node` carries `Reserved` (placements without an allocation), which `ListRuntimeNodes` already counts.\n- The free-slot rule also requires `Reserved == 0` on the node. A later scan keeps the slot free once the placed Session has its sandbox.\n- `docs/sandbox-provider.md` and its Chinese mirror state the condition.\n\n## Tests\n\n`TestFreeSlotWaitsForPlacedSession`: an allocation idle for 3 minutes on a node that is full only because of a waiting placement is refused (`ErrNotIdle`). It fails without the new condition. Ran `go test ./internal/persistence/postgres/deploymentpg -run 'TestPressure|TestFreeSlot|Suspension|Suspend'`, `go test ./internal/deployment/...` and `go vet ./...` for `services/core`.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/MiniMax-AI/codesmith/OpenAgentCore/pr/811?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795189084&installation_model_id=427615&pr_number=811&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=MiniMax-AI%2FOpenAgentCore&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FMiniMax-AI%2FOpenAgentCore%2Fpull%2F811&signature=256a2d67047b6041d139be87e38f4595c1eb1b45ed2d156de2e15bf3dff94a56\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
